                <pb facs="0256" n="222" sameAs="frus:frus1870/pg222"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Received at Washington August 22,
                        1870.]</seg></opener>
                <head>Mr. Von Thiele to Baron Gerolt.</head>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">North German Legation at Washington:</hi></p>
                <p>The bearer of a flag of truce, carrying a white flag, accompanied by a trumpeter
                    sounding his trumpet, who, at a slow pace, approached the French outposts, to
                    deliver messages from French surgeons in behalf of wounded Frenchmen, on the
                    19th of this month, has been fired at by all the French patrols he met, so that
                    he was obliged to return after his trumpeter had been severely wounded. We
                    solemnly protest against this breach of international law.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>VON THIELE.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
